      "content": "Combining caffeine and green tea extract can be effective for boosting metabolism, but since you already consume 4–5 cups of coffee, adding supplements increases your total intake significantly. A common effective and safe range is around 400 mg of caffeine total from all sources per day and 200–500 mg of green tea extract, though the specific efficacy depends on your individual metabolism. Because you have a high preference for coffee, exceeding the general daily caffeine limit of 400 mg could lead to jitters, anxiety, or even heart palpitations. It is crucial to monitor your body's response closely and consult a healthcare professional before stacking these stimulants, especially if you have underlying health conditions.",
