    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Pushing the upper limits of caffeine and green tea extract beyond standard guidelines even for short-term use carries significant risks, including heart palpitations, severe anxiety, and potential hypertension. Most medical authorities recommend a strict daily maximum of 400 mg of caffeine regardless of tolerance, and green tea extract doses above 500 mg can trigger toxic effects like liver damage or excessive stimulation. Using substances aggressively in pursuit of maximum fat burning often leads to a \"crash\" after the temporary boost wears off, which can set you back and disrupt the very weight loss progress you aim for. For sustainable and safe results, it is far better to focus on consistent nutritional habits and progressive training rather than escalating stimulant intake.",
